        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(sandbox): add skipSkillsSync config option to suppress skill sync",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nSkills are copied into the sandbox workspace on every sandbox setup. For users who do not use skills or have already deployed them through other means, this sync is unnecessary overhead.\n\nRelated: #97638\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAdds skipSkillsSync as an optional boolean under agents.defaults.sandbox and agents.list[].sandbox, defaulting to false. Only file copying (syncSkillsToWorkspace) is skipped; skills eligibility computation and skills snapshot (prompt text + env overrides) are preserved so Agent prompts continue to advertise available skills.\n\n## User Impact\n\n```json5\n{ agents: { defaults: { sandbox: { skipSkillsSync: true } } } }\n```\n\nSafe-use contract: Skills must be preinstalled via setupCommand or docker.binds. The workspace bind mount at /workspace shadows image-baked content, so Dockerfile-baked skills alone are not sufficient. The skills snapshot provides prompt text and env overrides from the host session-start snapshot.\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Zod schema documentation (code)\n\nUpdated to accurately reflect the safe-use contract: setupCommand or docker.binds are the supported paths; image-baked content at /workspace/skills is not sufficient because the sandbox bind-mounts the host workspace over /workspace.\n\n### Code-level proof (no-rebuild)\n\n- resolveSandboxSkillRuntimeInputs conditionally preserves the host skillsSnapshot when skipSkillsSync=true (sandbox-skills.ts:141-143)\n- resolveSkillsPromptForRun uses snapshotPrompt directly (no filesystem access) when snapshotPrompt is present\n- applySkillEnvOverridesFromSnapshot extracts env vars from snapshot.skills (same source as live-loaded entries)\n- computeSandboxSkillsEligibility still runs even when skipSkillsSync=true (context.ts), eligibility flows to prompt\n- The command/system-prompt inspection path (commands-system-prompt.ts:91) skips container-only loading and falls through to host-side resolveReusableWorkspaceSkillSnapshot\n\n### Test coverage\n\n40 tests pass (4 test files, 0 failures):\n- preserves snapshot when skipSkillsSync enabled (2 test files, ro + rw modes)\n- drops snapshot when absent (regression guard)\n- eligibility preserved when sync skipped (both ro and rw modes)\n- existing test: sync IS called when skipSkillsSync absent (regression guard)\n\n### Changed files (11 files, ~+176/-31)\n\nsrc/config/types.agents-shared.ts — type definition\nsrc/config/zod-schema.agent-runtime.ts — Zod schema + corrected contract description\nsrc/agents/sandbox/types.ts — SandboxConfig, SandboxWorkspaceInfo, SandboxContext\nsrc/agents/sandbox/config.ts — config resolver\nsrc/agents/sandbox/context.ts — computeSandboxSkillsEligibility, skipSkillsSync propagation\nsrc/agents/sandbox.resolveSandboxContext.test.ts — integration tests\nsrc/agents/embedded-agent-runner/sandbox-skills.ts — conditional skillsSnapshot\nsrc/agents/embedded-agent-runner/sandbox-skills.test.ts — unit tests\nsrc/agents/cli-runner/prepare.ts — pass skipSkillsSync\nsrc/auto-reply/reply/commands-system-prompt.ts — skip container path when skipSkillsSync",
        "branch": "feat/skip-skills-sync",
